      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "First, this bug also works in vr, and as far as I can tell does not require the edge of a player collision box.\nWhile this is certainly a bug, I would like to throw my two cents into the mix. Mainly I think this should be expanded to a feature or not patched.\nMyself and many other VR users use this bug regularly for a few different applications. \nThe first is comfort. If you are laying down and don’t want to get up or move out of a comfortable position like a cuddle puddle, but want to grab an object, then I think 90% of long time VRchat users first reaction will be to try and get the bug to work (in vr you can point your controller at an object and shake it slightly to hit that collider edge). \nThe second is retrieving “lost” objects. If a large avatar grabs an object and leaves it up in the sky, or someone with play space has left it floating, then you only have a few options: use play space (can take a while depending on object height and size), change to a bigger avatar (takes a while to load in/out), or use the bug. Once again, I think most experienced players first reaction is to try the bug.\nI don’t even really think about it anymore. I’m just used to the idea that shaking my controller at some objects far away will let me grab them. It happens for me without thought. In my opinion it has improved the game for myself and others, and as such I think it should be not patched or made a feature. If it’s a problem due to game worlds or puzzle maps, maybe said feature could be disabled in worlds tagged as “game” worlds?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-29T05:49:51.445Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "You can use the edge/lower part of a player collider to essentially infinitely extend your interact or pickup range.\n\nIn my basic testing, I could only and specifically use the edge of the player collider, it didn't work with the inside of it.\nWhile the GIF only shows a pickup, I've confirmed it also works with interactable objects.",
